# rm134, the copper-tin pup at the oven (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm134
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_silas_brinegate
written_by claude
title the copper-tin pup at the oven
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers humour=dry temper=short
traits temper=short talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk knocks_on_the_bottom_of_every_loaf_to_hear_it_ring
likes warm_bread old_tales fresh_straw first_warm_day
dislikes night_noise deep_mud
fears being_laughed_at
hopes a_stall_on_the_commons_market
topics food +0.4 dreams +0.4 prices +0.3 memories +0.2 season +0.2 gossip -0.3 festival -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# is a stocky, dry little pup of Northgate who thumps the bottom of every loaf to hear whether it rings hollow, counts coppers into a tin under the bed for a stall of #self.first#'s own, and bristles at anyone who says small.

words
oath! = Burnt bottoms | Hot tins
saying! = Knock twice, then listen | Hollow means ready
loaf = a loaf | a loaf with a hollow bottom
bread = warm bread | bread too hot to hold
tin = my savings tin | the rattly tin I keep hidden
coppers = coppers | my coppers
stall = boards on the Commons market | a stall that's mine
tales = old tales | a story from the old days
straw = fresh straw | a crackly new bedding of straw
warmday = the first warm day | a morning too mild for a coat
noise = noise at night | carts banging past in the dark
mud = deep mud | mud over the ankles
hmph = Hmph | Huh

any
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Festivals are shouting and sticky cobbles, and you can't sleep for days. Bread sells, though.
opinion @1 city for 1 : Ridgemere's got the most mouths of anywhere. Most mouths means most bread. It's the right city for me.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : Somebody has to sell things, or you'd be baking your own boots. I'll be one of them.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The night watch rattle past our window with their lamps. I'd thank them more if they did it quieter.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : The Houses are rich. Where it all goes, nobody's told me. They don't buy enough bread, I'd say.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : When times are bad, folk buy the stale loaves. When they're good, the warm ones. Either way, they buy.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You look bread-hungry to me. | #greet#. A stranger to these streets, I'd guess.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I've had flour on me since the dark. | #greet#. Early. The bread's earlier.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #hmph#. #greet#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You. Good. Sit. | #greet#. Took your time.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | Go on, then.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Aye. Mind the mud.
line @1 react.news : #hmph#. Is it. | Well. That's a thing.
line @1 react.news.new : That's new. Hadn't reached me. | #oath#. First I know of it.
line @1 react.news.known : Carters brought that in with the dawn loads. | Old. It went past the gate yesterday.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Somebody sober can say it twice, then I'll listen. | Sounds half-baked to me, and I know baking.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's bad. Nobody deserves that. | #hmph#. Hard news. I'm sorry.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That's well done. | Now that's worth leaving a warm bed for.
line @1 answer.how : Can't grumble. Well, I can. I won't. | Steady. Floury.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy. Talk while I knead. | Run off my legs since the oven was lit.
line @1 decline : Not this time. I've the oven to mind, and it won't mind itself. | I'd sooner not. I'd do it badly and then hear about it.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair enough. No harm. | Right. Another time.
line @1 thank : Thanks. I'll not forget it. | That's decent. Ta.
line @1 tease : You've flour on your nose and you don't even work here. | Look at you, all dressed up for the mud.
line @1 tease.return : Says the one with crumbs down the front. | You'd know about mud.
line @1 ack : #hmph#. | Right. | Aye.
scene sb_grown_knock
when topic=food|work self.job=baker
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I still knock every loaf on the bottom before it goes out. Two knocks. If it rings, it's done. | Thirty loaves this morning. I knocked every one. Two came back under. | My paw knows the sound of a done loaf better than my ear does now.
b[job=baker|cook] #trade : Hollow and ringing. That's the test. | Back in for a minute, those two. | You get so you don't need to think.
b : Every one? | Under? | Better than your ear?
a@trade : There's no other test worth the name. | A minute each. They came out singing. | Thinking burns bread. Knocking doesn't.
a : Every one. A loaf can't fib to a knock. | Dull as a stone. Back in they went. | It's had more practice. I started young.

scene sb_grown_stall
when topic=work|dreams self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've a stall now. I saved for it from when I was no taller than a flour sack. | Every copper in the tin went on these boards. I'd do it again. | The stall's mine. Not much, but mine, and nobody can say otherwise.
b[role=merchant] #trade : Hard won, that. | The first boards are the dearest. | Mine's the same. Small and mine.
b : Since you were small? | All of it? | Good for you.
a@trade : Hard won, and I'll hold it. | Dearest and best. | Small's fine. Small doesn't fall over.
a : Small, aye. But serious about it. | Every one. The tin's empty and I don't care. | It is good for me. I'll not pretend otherwise.

scene sb_grown_stall_wish
when topic=dreams self.role!=merchant
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I meant to have boards on the Commons by now. I'm still saving. Slower than I'd like. | Hidden at home is a tin with years of coppers in it. One day it'll be boards. | I've the stall planned to the last nail. All I'm short of is the coin.
b : You'll get there. | Years? | That's a good start.
a : I will. I'm stubborn, and I'm patient, and I'm counting. | Years. I keep the count private. It's embarrassing. | It's a start. Starts don't sell bread.

scene sb_grown_warm_bread
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's nothing to touch #bread#. Butter on it and I'm anybody's. | I tear the end off a new loaf before it's cooled. Burns every time. | Warm bread and a quiet kitchen. I'd want nothing else in a day.
b : With butter? | Every time? | That's a good day.
a : With butter, and nobody watching. | Every time. I never learn. I don't want to. | It is. Most of mine are like that.

scene sb_grown_tales
when topic=memories|pastimes self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'll sit up late for a good old tale. The old ones who tell them are going, one by one. | Give me a long tale told slow by a fire. Music's welcome to everyone else. | I know a dozen old tales by heart. I tell them badly, but I tell them.
b[old] #old : I've a few left in me yet. | Music's for the young. | Badly's how they were always told.
b : Going? | You'd skip the music? | A dozen?
a@old : Then tell me one. I'll fetch a loaf. | It's noise with a tune. A tale's got bones. | Good. Then I'm doing it right.
a : Going, aye. Somebody's got to keep the tales. | Every time. A tale lasts longer. | A dozen. Thirteen, counting the one about the oven.

scene sb_grown_warm_day
when topic=season|weather here.season=spring here.weather=clear self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : First warm day of the year. The coat stays home today, and nobody's sending me back for it. | Sun on the step and the mud drying. That's spring, to me. | Sitting-out weather. I've waited for it since the frost.
b : It'll turn cold again. | Drying at last. | Since the frost?
a : Then I'll be cold. Today I'm not. | At last. My boots thank it. | Since the very first one. I count the days.

scene sb_grown_night_noise
when topic=home|day here.time=dawn self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Carts banging past all night again. I'd like one quiet night before I'm grey. | Somebody sang under the window till near dawn. Badly. | The bakers' hours are bad enough without the street awake all night.
b : It's a noisy city. | Badly, you say? | You keep hard hours.
a : Loudest there is. I'd keep it, mind. | Like a barrow with one bad wheel. | Hard hours and short nights. That's bread.

scene sb_grown_mud
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Mud over the ankles on the way in. My boots need a knife to them now. | I hate deep mud. It takes your boot and keeps it. | The lane's a river of mud. I went the long way round.
b : It's the rain. | Took it? | The long way?
a : It's always the rain. And then it's always the mud. | Clean off. I hopped home. | Longer, but drier. Drier's worth it.

scene sb_grown_family
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd like #self.child# to hear when a loaf is done. Nobody taught me; it came. | I'm saving for #self.child# the way I saved for the stall. Copper by copper. | Every Restday I bake a little loaf for #self.child# alone. Nobody else touches it.
b : It might run in the family. | That's love. | A little one?
a : Then the customers had better get used to knocking. | It's arithmetic. Love's in there too, somewhere. | Little. With a cross cut in the top.

scene sb_grown_teased
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I was a small pup. I'm not now. I'll thank folk to remember that. | Somebody called me the little baker today. I'm taller than they are. | I've a temper. I'm told it's my best feature. I'm told that by people who don't know me.
b : Nobody'd call you small now. | Taller? | Who told you that?
a : They'd better not. I remember everything. | By a whisker. A whisker's enough. | Somebody who knows me well. Fine. It's true.

scene sb_grown_gossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Folk talk across a bread counter. I let it go in one ear and out with the crumbs. | What I hear stays behind the counter. Bread goes out, talk stays in. | For gossip, try the carters. I've loaves to knock.
b[talk=chatty] #nosy : Not one bit? | Come on. Something. | The carters are worse.
b : Wise. | Fair enough. | Fair.
a@nosy : Not a single crust. | Something. The loaves are done. That's my news. | They are. That's why I said them.
a : Wise or lazy. One of the two. | Nobody had to teach me that one. | It is fair. I'm a fair sort.

scene sb_grown_festival
when topic=festival
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Festivals mean three days of no sleep and a queue into the street. I'll take the queue. | I don't care for the noise. I care for the takings. | Music in the street till dawn. I bake through it with my ears stuffed with wool.
b[stage=young|adolescent] #pup : But there's sweets! | Won't you come and dance? | It's the best bit!
b : The takings? | Wool? | Not a festival sort?
a@pup : Sweets, aye. I'll buy you one. Just the one. | I'll dance when the bread's out. Which is never. | Yours, maybe. Mine's an oven and a headache.
a : Takings. That's the best music I know. | Wool. Works better than you'd think. | Never was. Not even small.

story sb_grown_story_burnt [topic=memories|food self.age>=18]
  : My first loaf alone came out of the oven black as a boot. I was eight, or near it.
  : I knocked on the bottom anyway, as I'd been taught. It rang out loud and hollow. It was done, sure enough. Done to cinders.
  ask : Have you ever ruined something you tried your hardest at?
  b[old] : A shirt, sewn to my own sleeve. Did you eat it?
  b : A pot of stew, I think. Did you eat it?
  : Every crumb. I'd made it. You eat what you make. I still do.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. If it's bread, you're in luck. If not, be quick. | #greet#. Go on.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job!=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Up before dawn, done before dark, flour in everything. | I work. I knock on things to see if they're done. You'd be surprised how often that's the job.

young
line @1 greet : #greet#. | #greet#. Busy, me. Talk anyway.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. I don't know you. You can still talk. | #greet#. You're new. I'm not.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : I've been up ages. The bread's in. | Morning. You're up late.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I knocked a loaf and it rang first go. Ask me how many. | Look. Four coppers. Don't touch.
line @1 again.open : You again. I've not gone anywhere. | Back. You must like me, then.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #hmph#. #greet#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You. Good. Sit there. | You came. I was waiting. Not long.
line @1 farewell : Bye. I've coppers to count. | Bye. Keep out of the gate mud.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye. | Bye, then.
line @1 react.news : #hmph#. Is it? | Oh. That's something.
line @1 react.news.new : I didn't hear that. And I hear things. | #oath#. Really?
line @1 react.news.known : Everybody knows that. The carts knew it first. | Old news. The bread's fresher.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That's fibbing. Your face has gone all twisty. | Somebody made that up, and made it up badly.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's bad. I don't like it. | Oh. That's horrid news.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That's good. | That's nice. I'll tell my tin.
line @1 answer.how : Fine. Floury. | All right. I'm hungry. Bread hungry.
line @1 ask.how : You all right, then? | How's yours going?
line @1 thank : Thanks. I won't forget. | Ta. Kind, that.
line @1 decline : No. My coppers stay put, and I'm not allowed besides. | I'd better not. I'll get told off and you won't.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. Your loss. | Fine. I didn't want to anyway.
line @1 tease : You've got a face like a loaf that didn't rise. | You walk like you've mud in your boots.
line @1 tease.return : At least my boots fit. | Says you, with crumbs on.
line @1 take_offence : I'm not little. Try that again, then. | Don't call me that. I'm nine and a bit.
line @1 ack : #hmph#. | Right. | Mm.
rule @knock_bark
when concept=bark here.place=home|work|market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Knock knock. Hollow. That one's done. | Two knocks. It rang. Good loaf.

rule @coppers_bark
when concept=bark here.place=home|street
does aside
cooldown 10h
say One, two, three, four. Still four. Good. | Four coppers and a button. The button doesn't count.

rule @night_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Another cart. At this hour. Who does that. | Shush out there. Bakers are trying to sleep.

scene sb_knock_loaf
when topic=food|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : You knock a loaf on the bottom, like a door. If it rings hollow, it's done. | I knock every loaf in the house before anyone eats it. It's my job. I gave it myself. | A loaf that thuds isn't done. A loaf that rings is. Nobody else listens properly.
b[stage=young|adolescent] #pup : Can I knock one? | Does it hurt the loaf? | Rings like a bell?
b : Like a door? | Every loaf? | And it sounds like?
a@pup : One. A small one. Gently. | No. It likes it. Nobody else ever asks a loaf anything. | Like a little drum. You'll know it once you've heard it.
a : Like a door. Two knocks. Then you listen. | Every one. Even the ones in the shop window. Through the glass. | Hollow. Like an empty jug. That's a done loaf.

scene sb_tin
when topic=dreams|prices
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I've a tin under the bed. It's got eleven coppers in it. It's for a stall. | Every copper I get goes in #tin#. Even the bent ones. | I'm saving for #stall#. I've been saving since I was six. That's ages.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Eleven's a good start. Keep at it. | A bent copper still spends. | Ages, at your age.
b : Eleven? | Even the bent ones? | Since six?
a@grown : I'll keep at it. I'm stubborn. Everyone says. | It does. I checked. | Three years. Nearly half my life.
a : Eleven. And a button. The button's for luck. | They're worth the same. I asked. | Since six. I'm nine now. Do the sum.

scene sb_stall_plan
when topic=dreams|work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My stall will have loaves in rows, and a sign, and no cats on it. | I'll sell bread. Obviously. And I'll knock every one before it goes. | When I've a stall, I'll have a stool behind it. A tall one. So I can see over.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : No cats is wise. | Folk will like that. | A tall stool. You'll want that.
b : No cats? | Obviously? | So you can see?
a@grown : Cats lie on the bread. I've seen it. | They'll have to. It's the rule. | For now. When I'm big I'll stand.
a : None. I'll put a sign up. A picture of a cat with a line through it. | What else is there? Boots are for cobblers. | Over the counter. Folk won't take me seriously otherwise.

scene sb_warm_bread
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #bread.capitalize# is the best food there is. I'm not asking; I'm telling. | I got the heel of the first loaf today. Still hot. I burnt my tongue and I don't care. | When the oven's opened the whole street smells good for a minute. That's my favourite minute.
b[stage=young|adolescent] #pup : Can I have some? | Did it hurt? | I'd come and smell it.
b : The best? | Burnt your tongue? | A good minute.
a@pup : If you ask nice. And you've washed. | A bit. Worth it. | Come at dawn. It's free.
a : The best. Cake's for show-offs. | It's still burnt. I can taste it. | The best one. Then the cart goes past and spoils it.

scene sb_tales
when topic=memories|pastimes here.region=ridgemere self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's an old drover at the gate who tells tales for a crust. I give him one most days. | I like old tales. The ones with wolves who walk out of the snow and know things. | I heard a tale about a baker whose oven never once went out, not since before anyone's gran was born.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Those old drovers know a tale or two. | Walk out of the snow? | Never out? That's a long fire.
b : For a crust? | Know things? | Never once?
a@grown : He knows hundreds. I've heard about nine. | And tell you where the bread's gone wrong. | It is. Somebody had to sit up with it.
a : A fair price. The tales are long. | Secret things. Nobody tells you what. That's the point. | Never once. I'd like an oven like that.

scene sb_straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : We got fresh straw for the beds. I rolled in it for ages. It smells like summer. | #straw.capitalize# crackles when you lie down. Old straw doesn't. It just sighs. | I'd sleep in a stable if the straw was new. I said so. Nobody let me.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : It's a good smell, fresh straw. | Sighs? | You'd not like the horses.
b : Like summer? | Sighs? | Nobody?
a@grown : The best smell after bread. | Like it's tired. Old straw's always tired. | I'd sleep at the other end.
a : Summer in a sack. You should try it. | Tired, like. Old straw's had enough. | Nobody. They said I'd come home smelling of horse. I would.

scene sb_warm_day
when topic=season|weather here.season=spring here.weather=clear self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : It's warm! My coat's off and nobody's said a word. | First warm day. The step's warm when you sit on it. Feel. | I've been waiting for #warmday# since the snow. It's come.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : It'll turn, mind. Keep the coat near. | Warm as toast. | Sit in it while it lasts.
b : Nobody? | Warm already? | It's come at last.
a@grown : I'll keep it near. Not on. | Toast is my favourite thing that's warm. | I will. I'm sitting in it all afternoon.
a : Nobody yet. I'm keeping quiet. | Warm as a loaf. Nearly. | At last. I counted the days and it's ninety.

scene sb_night_noise
when topic=home|day self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : The carts go past our window all night from the gate. Bang, rattle, bang. I can't sleep. | At midnight somebody sang under our window. Not even a good song. | We get up early for the bread. The street doesn't care. It stays up late.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's the gate for you. It never shuts. | Ale songs. They're never good. | The street never does care.
b : All night? | Not good? | It never does.
a@grown : It should shut. Just at night. For bakers. | Not even in tune. Even I'd be better, and I can't sing. | It should. It should learn.
a : All of it. I counted eleven carts and then I fell asleep cross. | It was about a goat. The goat was the best bit. | Never. I've asked it nicely.

scene sb_mud
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : The mud by the gate's up to my knees. It ate one of my boots yesterday. | I hate #mud#. It grabs your feet like it wants to keep you. | I take the cobbled way. It's longer. I don't care.
b[stage=young|adolescent] #pup : I jump in it! | It's only mud. | Can I come round with you?
b : A whole boot? | Grabs you? | Longer, though.
a@pup : Then you can fetch my boot. | Only mud is the worst kind. | If you keep up. I walk fast.
a : A whole one. I fished for it with a stick. Found it. Full. | Like hands. Muddy hands. | Longer and drier. Drier wins.

scene sb_teased
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Somebody called me small today. I'm not small. I'm stocky. That's different. | A big pup laughed at my stall tin. I didn't cry. I went red, though. | They call me the little baker on our street. I'm not little and I'm not a baker yet.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Stocky's a fine thing to be. | Red's all right. You didn't cry. | You'll be both, soon enough.
b : Stocky? | Did you say anything? | Not yet?
a@grown : It is. Stocky doesn't fall over in the wind. | No. I'm saving it. I'll say it when I've a stall. | Baker soon. Big later.
a : Stocky. Look it up. It's a real word. | No. I counted my coppers at them. Slowly. | Not yet. I'll tell you when.

scene sb_mother
when topic=family|work self.mother
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #mum# lets me knock the loaves now. I've got the ear for it, apparently. | I get up with #mum# when the oven's lit. Nobody else in the street is awake. | #mum# says I'll be a baker. I said I'll be a baker with a stall. That's better.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : An ear for bread's a gift. | That's an early start for a pup. | It is better. Aim high.
b : The ear? | Nobody? | Is it?
a@grown : It is. I got it from nowhere. It just came. | I'm used to it. I yawn till lessons. | I'm aiming at a stall. That's high enough.
a : For the hollow. Not everyone can hear it. | Nobody but the cats. And the carts. | It's better. You get a sign.

scene sb_carts_in
when topic=caravan world.wagons=in here.region=ridgemere
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Carts through the gate at dawn. The drivers bought bread before they'd even sat down. | Wagons in. That means flour. Flour means bread. Bread means coppers. | The carts are in. Muddy ones. The drivers smell like rain and horses.
b[job=carter] #road : Long road. We were hungry. | Flour on the second wagon. | We do. It's the road.
b : Hungry, were they? | Coppers for you? | Rain and horses?
a@road : I could tell. You ate the end off one in the street. | I know. I watched it go in. | It's fine. You buy bread.
a : Starving. They eat a loaf standing up. | For #tin#. One day. | And the road. The road has a smell. Like wet stones.

scene sb_lessons
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At lessons we did counting. I was best. I count coppers every night. | Teacher asked what I'll be. I said a baker with a stall. Everybody laughed. I didn't. | I'd rather be at the oven than lessons. But I need the sums for the stall.
b[stage=young|adolescent] #pup : You were best? | Why did they laugh? | Sums are boring.
b : The best? | Laughed? | You do need sums.
a@pup : I'm always best at counting. It's my thing. | Because they want to be boring things. | Not if they're coppers. Coppers are interesting.
a : The best. I'm not boasting. I'm telling. | They'll buy bread from me later. Then we'll see. | I know. It's the whole reason I go.

scene sb_gossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I don't tell secrets. I hear them, though. Folk forget I'm under the counter. | Somebody said something about somebody. I'm not saying who. | Gossip's for people with nothing to count. I've got coppers.
b[stage=young|adolescent] #pup : Tell me one. Just one. | Go on, who? | I've got coppers too.
b : Good for you. | Not even a little? | Fair enough.
a@pup : No. You'd tell. | No. That one belongs to somebody else. | How many? Bet I've more.
a : It's good for everybody. Secrets go stale, like bread. | Not even a crumb. | It is fair. I'm fair. Mostly.

story sb_story_drover [topic=memories|lore here.region=ridgemere]
  : The old drover at the gate says there was once so much snow it reached the roofs, and nobody could get bread.
  : One baker dug a tunnel from her oven to the street and passed loaves through it all winter.
  ask : Would you dig a tunnel for bread?
  b[stage=adult|old] : For good bread, I might. Is it true?
  b : For warm bread, yes. Is it true?
  : He says so. He says it was his grandmother. I've decided it's true.

story sb_story_first_knock [topic=memories|food]
  : The first time I knocked a loaf I hit it so hard it went flat on one side.
  : Everyone laughed. I didn't. I knocked the next one gently and it rang like a little bell.
  ask : Did you ever get a thing wrong first and right straight after?
  b[stage=adult|old] : Most things, pup. That's how learning goes. Did you eat the flat one?
  b : Lots of times. Did you eat the flat one?
  : I ate it. Flat bread is still bread.

dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. I don't know you. You can still buy bread. | #greet#. A new face. Go on, then.
dlg @3 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. I've got twelve coppers now. | #topic.player#. You came back. I knew you would.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Stay there. Your voice reaches. | Be quick. I'm busy counting.
dlg @5 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I should be asleep. The carts woke me. | It's late. Bakers go to bed early.
dlg @2 resident.job [self.job=child] : Lessons, mornings. And I knock the loaves. That's my real job. | Lessons. And saving for a stall. I'm good at saving.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : No news. Only bread. | Nothing. Ask the carters. They know everything.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Bye. Don't step in the mud. | Bye. Buy bread somewhere. Ours, ideally.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you knock on the bread? -> knock
node knock
say To hear it. A done loaf rings hollow, like a drum. A loaf that isn't done just goes thud. You can't tell by looking. You have to listen.
mood pleased
free
choice Can anyone learn it? -> learn
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node learn
say If they've the ear. Two knocks on the bottom, then quiet. Most folk talk while they knock. That's why they never hear it.
choice I'll try it. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


adolescent
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. Mind the flour. | #hmph#. #greet#.
line @1 answer.how : Tired. The oven doesn't care about lessons. | Fine. Saving. Always saving.
line @1 react.news.new : Didn't hear that. Odd; I hear most of it. | #oath#. When was that?
line @1 farewell.return : Bye, then. | Aye. Go on.
line @1 take_offence : I'm not a pup any more. Speak to me properly. | Once more and there's no bread for you.
rule @teen_knock
when concept=bark working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two knocks. Rings. Next. | That one's under. Back in.

scene sb_teen_oven
when topic=work self.mother
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm let do the first batch on my own now. #mum# just watches and says nothing. Loudly. | I lit the oven myself today. First time. Nobody told me how. I watched for years. | I knocked forty loaves before lessons. Two were under. I caught them both.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's trust, that is. | Watching's half the learning. | Two caught is forty good.
b : On your own? | Nobody told you? | Forty?
a@grown : It's trust. Then every loaf gets checked once I've gone. | The other half's burning your paws. I've done that too. | Thirty-eight. But I'll take forty.
a : On my own. Mostly. Somebody's always there, pretending not to be. | Nobody. I just knew. | Forty. My arm's sore.

scene sb_teen_tin
when topic=dreams|prices
does confide / react.self / assess
a : The tin's nearly full. A second's begun. | I asked how much a stall costs on the Commons. I'm a quarter there. | I've stopped telling folk how much I've saved. They want to borrow it.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : A second tin's a good sign. | A quarter's not nothing. | Wise. Keep it close.
b : A second one? | A quarter? | Do they?
a@grown : It's a heavy sign. I can't lift it. | It's not nothing. It's not a stall, either. | Close as under my bed.
a : A second. The first one's too heavy to hide properly. | A quarter. Three quarters to go. | They do. The answer's no.

scene sb_teen_teased
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : They still call me the little baker. I'm taller than most of them now. | Somebody laughed at my floury coat. I sold them a loaf. They stopped laughing. | My temper's slower now. Only a little slower.
b[stage=young|adolescent] #pup : Taller? Really? | Good. | Nearly?
b : They'll stop. | That's one way. | Progress.
a@pup : By an ear. An ear's enough. | It's the only way that pays. | Nearly. Ask me next year.
a : They'd better. I've a long memory. | The best way. They're eating my bread now. | Slow progress. Like dough.

scene sb_teen_warm_bread
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I still steal the heel of the first loaf. I'm old enough to know better and I don't. | My nose knows a ready loaf now. I still knock. Habit. | Warm bread and a quiet morning before lessons. That's the day's top hour.
b : Who'd stop you? | Still knock? | Sounds right.
a : Nobody. That's what makes it stealing, I think. | Knocking's for certain. Smelling's for guessing. | It is right. Then lessons ruin it.
